Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:12:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] the hunt, second look at the fact set: 18 right, 0
 wrong, 13 gaps of 31 under the real priors home (REUSED, dev-like)

Wrong answers read sentence by sentence and traced to causes: a fragment cut by the splitter cleared the "bare he follows another subject" guard; title words and Roman numerals dropped out of the anchor ("Divine Comedy", "World War I"); the name-folding rule folded a year into an unrelated date; a day and month with no year now take the sentence's earlier year; do-support, a participle hung by the unspecified label, and a phrase hung from a full stop under the real parser; a settlement noun carries the locative ("the city of Stagira"); extraction residue (nbsp, run-together sentences, a link's target before its display text) cleaned in the view, never in the address. Hunt, source and conversation suites pass under both priors homes; the three older hunt tests that failed on the real parser pass. The demo reads the latest run. Results v4 to v11 kept; RESULTS-ANSWER.md has the v7 to v11 table and root causes. Not pushed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
